{
  "description": "Conformance corpus for rendering a `typeRef`. Every generator that turns a type reference into text asserts against this file, so the two cannot drift apart and, more to the point, cannot drift together.",
  "notes": [
    "`typegen` and `docgen` are two resolvers of one grammar. When the array-of-union precedence bug shipped, both were wrong in the same way, so a test asserting only that they AGREE would have passed. Each case therefore pins the expected text explicitly.",
    "`typescript` is what `typegen` emits and what `docgen` puts inside its fenced TypeScript signature. `markdown` is what `docgen` puts in a parameter or field table, where type names are backticked and pipes are escaped for the table.",
    "An element type that is a union or an optional must be parenthesised before `[]`: `string | number[]` is a union with an array, not an array of a union. It compiles, which is why it went unnoticed.",
    "The string form is a grammar: `union := postfix ('|' postfix)*`, `postfix := primary ('[]' | '?')*`, `primary := name | '(' union ')'`. `[]` and `?` bind tighter than `|`. A string outside the grammar, such as a generic, is one opaque name emitted verbatim.",
    "Accepted type words resolve to one meaning everywhere: `int`, `integer`, and `float` to `number`; `bool` to `boolean`; `array` to `any[]`; `object` to `Record<string, any>`; `function` to `(...args: any[]) => any`. A function type is parenthesised as an array element or a union member, as TypeScript requires.",
    "`canonical`, when present, lists the non-canonical spellings `lint` reports for the case (an accepted type word, or `T?` for the optional suffix). A case without it is already canonical."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a primitive",
      "ref": "string",
      "typescript": "string",
      "markdown": "`string`"
    },
    {
      "name": "a custom type name",
      "ref": "Player",
      "typescript": "Player",
      "markdown": "`Player`"
    },
    {
      "name": "the array shorthand",
      "ref": "Player[]",
      "typescript": "Player[]",
      "markdown": "`Player`[]"
    },
    {
      "name": "the array object form",
      "ref": {
        "array": "Player"
      },
      "typescript": "Player[]",
      "markdown": "`Player`[]"
    },
    {
      "name": "a union",
      "ref": {
        "union": [
          "string",
          "number"
        ]
      },
      "typescript": "string | number",
      "markdown": "`string` \\| `number`"
    },
    {
      "name": "an array of a union is parenthesised",
      "ref": {
        "array": {
          "union": [
            "string",
            "number"
          ]
        }
      },
      "typescript": "(string | number)[]",
      "markdown": "(`string` \\| `number`)[]"
    },
    {
      "name": "an array of an optional is parenthesised",
      "ref": {
        "array": {
          "optional": "Player"
        }
      },
      "typescript": "(Player | undefined)[]",
      "markdown": "(`Player` \\| `undefined`)[]"
    },
    {
      "name": "a union of arrays keeps each element unparenthesised",
      "ref": {
        "union": [
          {
            "array": "string"
          },
          "number"
        ]
      },
      "typescript": "string[] | number",
      "markdown": "`string`[] \\| `number`"
    },
    {
      "name": "a map",
      "ref": {
        "map": "Player"
      },
      "typescript": "Record<string, Player>",
      "markdown": "Record<string, `Player`>"
    },
    {
      "name": "the string form binds [] tighter than |",
      "ref": "string | number[]",
      "typescript": "string | number[]",
      "markdown": "`string` \\| `number`[]"
    },
    {
      "name": "the string form groups with parentheses",
      "ref": "(string | number)[]",
      "typescript": "(string | number)[]",
      "markdown": "(`string` \\| `number`)[]"
    },
    {
      "name": "a nested array shorthand",
      "ref": "Player[][]",
      "typescript": "Player[][]",
      "markdown": "`Player`[][]"
    },
    {
      "name": "the ? suffix is an optional",
      "ref": "Player?",
      "typescript": "Player | undefined",
      "markdown": "`Player` \\| `undefined`",
      "canonical": ["T?"]
    },
    {
      "name": "an optional array",
      "ref": "string[]?",
      "typescript": "string[] | undefined",
      "markdown": "`string`[] \\| `undefined`",
      "canonical": ["T?"]
    },
    {
      "name": "an array of optionals",
      "ref": "string?[]",
      "typescript": "(string | undefined)[]",
      "markdown": "(`string` \\| `undefined`)[]",
      "canonical": ["T?"]
    },
    {
      "name": "int is a number",
      "ref": "int",
      "typescript": "number",
      "markdown": "`number`",
      "canonical": ["int"]
    },
    {
      "name": "integer is a number",
      "ref": "integer",
      "typescript": "number",
      "markdown": "`number`",
      "canonical": ["integer"]
    },
    {
      "name": "float is a number",
      "ref": "float",
      "typescript": "number",
      "markdown": "`number`",
      "canonical": ["float"]
    },
    {
      "name": "bool is a boolean",
      "ref": "bool",
      "typescript": "boolean",
      "markdown": "`boolean`",
      "canonical": ["bool"]
    },
    {
      "name": "array is an array of any",
      "ref": "array",
      "typescript": "any[]",
      "markdown": "`any`[]",
      "canonical": ["array"]
    },
    {
      "name": "object is a string-keyed map of any",
      "ref": "object",
      "typescript": "Record<string, any>",
      "markdown": "Record<string, `any`>",
      "canonical": ["object"]
    },
    {
      "name": "the function[] shorthand is parenthesised",
      "ref": "function[]",
      "typescript": "((...args: any[]) => any)[]",
      "markdown": "(`(...args: any[]) => any`)[]",
      "canonical": ["function"]
    },
    {
      "name": "a function in a union is parenthesised",
      "ref": {
        "union": [
          "function",
          "string"
        ]
      },
      "typescript": "((...args: any[]) => any) | string",
      "markdown": "(`(...args: any[]) => any`) \\| `string`",
      "canonical": ["function"]
    },
    {
      "name": "type words resolve inside a string union",
      "ref": "int | bool",
      "typescript": "number | boolean",
      "markdown": "`number` \\| `boolean`",
      "canonical": ["int", "bool"]
    },
    {
      "name": "type words resolve inside the object form",
      "ref": {
        "map": "int[]"
      },
      "typescript": "Record<string, number[]>",
      "markdown": "Record<string, `number`[]>",
      "canonical": ["int"]
    },
    {
      "name": "the open primitives pass through",
      "ref": "unknown | any",
      "typescript": "unknown | any",
      "markdown": "`unknown` \\| `any`"
    },
    {
      "name": "a bare function is an untyped callback",
      "ref": "function",
      "typescript": "(...args: any[]) => any",
      "markdown": "`(...args: any[]) => any`",
      "canonical": ["function"]
    },
    {
      "name": "a function with a signature",
      "ref": {
        "function": {
          "params": [
            {
              "name": "cell",
              "type": "number"
            }
          ],
          "returns": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "typescript": "(cell: number) => boolean",
      "markdown": "`(cell: number) => boolean`"
    },
    {
      "name": "a signature with an optional union parameter and no return keeps its pipes inside one code span",
      "ref": {
        "function": {
          "params": [
            {
              "name": "key",
              "type": {
                "union": [
                  "string",
                  "number"
                ]
              },
              "required": false
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typescript": "(key?: string | number) => void",
      "markdown": "`(key?: string \\| number) => void`"
    },
    {
      "name": "an optional function is parenthesised so undefined does not join its return type",
      "ref": {
        "optional": "function"
      },
      "typescript": "((...args: any[]) => any) | undefined",
      "markdown": "(`(...args: any[]) => any`) \\| `undefined`",
      "canonical": ["function"]
    },
    {
      "name": "an array of functions is parenthesised",
      "ref": {
        "array": {
          "function": {
            "returns": "void"
          }
        }
      },
      "typescript": "(() => void)[]",
      "markdown": "(`() => void`)[]"
    },
    {
      "name": "a signature's variadic and reserved-word parameters stay legal",
      "ref": {
        "function": {
          "params": [
            { "name": "class", "type": "int" },
            { "name": "rest", "type": "string", "variadic": true }
          ],
          "returns": "bool"
        }
      },
      "typescript": "(class_: number, ...rest: string[]) => boolean",
      "markdown": "`(class_: number, ...rest: string[]) => boolean`",
      "canonical": ["int", "bool"]
    }
  ]
}
